Totals for representatives 216..323: 25,056 admissible singleton triples; 676,512 direction states; 524,016 rank-three states; 26,352 generalized-weight-admissible states. Every final state has external increment 0; the established reduction requires increment 5. Hence representatives 216..323 are excluded.

Together with the first-third and middle-third parent certificates on this branch, all 324 representatives are excluded. Full-class totals are 75,168 admissible singleton triples; 2,029,536 direction states; 1,561,464 rank-three states; 77,544 generalized-weight-admissible states; external increment census {0:77544}.

Ranks were computed modulo P=2^127-1. Lucas-Lehmer passed. The maximum squared relation-row norm in the final third is 36, and P^2 > 36^15, so the existing Hadamard argument certifies the modular rank decisions over Q.

The final-third computation was executed once with a self-contained exact reconstruction of current-main coordinate formulas and again through the committed verifier body against an API-compatible local shim exposing that reconstruction. All six subshard censuses agreed. No sampling or heuristic pruning was used.

Remaining bottleneck: this branch closes the second trivial-stabilizer (3,2,2,1) support class. The first order-1 class {1234,1235,1246,1367} and the final order-2 class {1234,1235,1267,1467} have exact certificates on divergent branches and are not assumed merged into main. The other unresolved k=5 arithmetic branches remain D=-2,(d_root,p)=(0,5) and D=-1,(d_root,p)=(0,6).
